  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The budget of Technex'23 is RRR thousand rupees. Since ICM is their flagship event, they will allocate **at least half** of their budget to it.\n\nThere are 555 other events planned under Technex'23.\n\nThe team wants to distribute the remaining amount **equally** among these.\n\nFind the **maximum** amount in rupees that could be allocated to each of the other five events.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single integer RRR, the budget of Technex'23 in thousand rupees.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single integer on a new line, the **maximum** amount in rupees that could be allocated to each of the other five events.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤R≤30001 \\leq R \\leq 30001≤R≤3000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n20\n43\n133",
        "output": "2000\n4300\n13300",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The budget of Technex'23 is 200002000020000 rupees. If ICM is allocated 100001000010000 rupees and the remaining 100001000010000 rupees is distributed among the other events, each will have a budget of 200020002000 rupees, which is the maximum possible.\nTest case 222: The budget of Technex'23 is 430004300043000 rupees. If 215002150021500 rupees is allocated to ICM, the rest of the events can each be alloted 430043004300 rupees.\nTest case 333: The budget of Technex'23 is 133000133000133000 rupees. If 665006650066500 rupees is allocated to ICM, the rest of the events can each be alloted 133001330013300 rupees."
      }
    ]
  },
